  "result": "I'd reply without any tool actions. There's no project to explore yet, and the spreadsheet they described is the whole current state.\n\n---\n\nThanks for sharing the spreadsheet. Here's what I see in it: each loan is a row with the seed, how many packets, who took them, and the dates out and back. About a third of the \"Date back\" cells are empty.\n\nThose blanks could mean a few different things, and the right tool depends heavily on which. Seed libraries also often work differently from book libraries: what comes back may be seeds saved from the harvest, months later, or nothing at all. So before I think about what to build, I'd like to understand the problem from your side.\n\nWhen the spreadsheet lets you down, what's actually happening? Tell me about a recent moment when you or another volunteer needed to know something and it didn't give you what you needed.",
